## Part 3 — The gap, stated plainly

Everything above is working around missing telemetry. Three changes would do more than
any query here:

1. **Enable 4688 with command-line auditing.** One GPO setting plus
   `ProcessCreationIncludeCmdLine_Enabled`. This is the single highest-value change
   available and costs almost nothing.
2. **Log firewall allows, at minimum on the perimeter and any segmentation boundary.**
   Deny-only logging means the successful intrusion is structurally invisible. Volume is
   the usual objection — sample or scope it rather than skipping it.
3. **PowerShell script block logging (4104).** Even partially, it recovers most of what
   attackers do after initial access.

Sysmon is the obvious fourth, but the three above are native, free, and defensible as
baseline hygiene in a way that deploying an agent sometimes is not.

Until then: authentication rarity is your detection, the firewall gives you timing
brackets, and 7045 is your execution proxy.
